module

public import Sheaf.Paper.DerivedHomMayerVietoris
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.Quasicoherent
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.Sheaf

/-! # Coherent modules on a ringed space

Source: Stacks Project, Modules, Tags 01BV (coherent), 01B5 (finite type), 01BE
(quasi-coherent); Schemes, Tag 01IA (blueprint: pqf-def-coherent).

The three notions of the node, on the carrier `SheafOfModules.{u} (moduleRings X)` shared
with the finite-presentation siblings (for a scheme `X`, `X.Modules` and
`SheafOfModules (moduleRings X.toRingedSpace)` are the same type):

- quasi-coherent is Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent` (Stacks 01BE: locally the
  cokernel of a map of free modules; the affine-local form `F|_U ≅ M~` of 01IA is a theorem
  about schemes, not a second definition);
- of finite type is Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` (Stacks 01B5: locally generated by
  finitely many sections, i.e. locally a quotient of `O_U^{⊕ n}`);
- coherent is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.IsCoherent` below (Stacks 01BV).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace

/-- A module `F` on a ringed space `X` (for a scheme, on `X.toRingedSpace`) is *coherent* if it
is of finite type (Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`) and for every open `U` and every
map `O_U^{⊕ n} ⟶ F|_U` the kernel is of finite type. Here `F|_U = F.over U` is the restriction
`SheafOfModules.overFunctor (moduleRings X) U` and `O_U^{⊕ n}` is the free module on
`ULift (Fin n)` over `(moduleRings X).over U`.
Source: Stacks Project, Modules, Tag 01BV (blueprint: pqf-def-coherent). -/
def IsCoherent (X : RingedSpace.{u}) (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (moduleRings X)) : Prop :=
  F.IsFiniteType ∧
    ∀ (U : Opens X) (n : ℕ)
      (f : SheafOfModules.free (R := (moduleRings X).over U) (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) ⟶ F.over U),
      (kernel f).IsFiniteType

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace
